# Implementation Plan: Comprehensive Systems Overhaul & Feature Polish

A holistic implementation roadmap completing and unifying the major partially-implemented and dormant systems in Tarmin 2: the Traveling NPC Merchant, Statue Encounters, Potions & Alchemy, Spell Inscription & Arcane Attunement, Twitchy Monster Attack Indicators & Active Parrying, and Weather Survival Exposure.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Traveling Merchant Combat Safety**: The Traveling Merchant roams corridors fighting monsters. If killed by roaming mobs, he drops a gold pouch and 2–3 high-tier wares on the floor, and a fresh merchant arrives on subsequent delves.
> - **Fast / Hectic Monster Attack Telegraphing**: Monster attack animations will be ultra-snappy (0.08s–0.12s total duration) so combat never stalls or feels sluggish, utilizing randomized variations (Eye Flare + Billboard Lunge, Retro Threat Aura pulse, or Screen-space Slash overlays).
> - **Scroll Inscription**: Reading scrolls remains an emergency free single-cast, while Inscribing commits the spell permanently into an open spellbook slot at the cost of 100% of the spell's MP.

